# NEBULA development overrides. Copy to your shell profile or export them before running `nebula`.
#
# NO SECRETS HERE. Provider API keys, ChatGPT tokens and Telegram bot tokens are entered in the dashboard and stored
# in the macOS Keychain. NEBULA never reads secrets from environment variables or .env files.

# A separate instance beside your normal install (own data dir, Keychain service, LaunchAgent and VM hostname).
# NEBULA_INSTANCE=dev

# Data and log directories. Normally derived from the instance; set them only for special setups.
# NEBULA_DATA_DIR="$HOME/Library/Application Support/NEBULA-dev"
# NEBULA_LOG_DIR="$HOME/Library/Application Support/NEBULA-dev/logs"

# Dashboard and API port (the remote gateway defaults to this port + 2).
# NEBULA_PORT=3200

# Allow the Vite dev server origin (`cd apps/dashboard && pnpm dev`) and tell the dev server where the API is.
# NEBULA_DEV_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5173
# NEBULA_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:3200

# Secret backend: keychain (default) or memory. 'memory' is for tests only: secrets are lost when the process exits.
# NEBULA_SECRET_BACKEND=keychain

# Use a different VM helper binary (for helper development).
# NEBULA_VM_HELPER=apps/host-vm-helper/.build/release/nebula-vm

# APNs topic (your app's bundle id) when push is configured without a topic setting.
# NEBULA_APNS_TOPIC=com.example.nebula
